<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nebiryraw I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nebiryraw I was a king of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-intermediate-period">Second Intermediate Period</a>, ruling from Thebes around 1600 BCE; in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-ryholt">Kim Ryholt</a>'s reconstruction he is one of the better-attested kings of the Sixteenth Dynasty, while others place him in the Seventeenth. He is named in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin-king-list">Turin King List</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> Juridical Stela, recording a legal settlement over the governorship of El-Kab, is dated to his first regnal year.</p></div>
